    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI updated the locality derivation in `OwnerMapper.locality()` to prefer the postcode over the city.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`:\n\n- Added a `REGION_POSTCODES` table (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099), mirroring the ranges already used for validation in `Postcodes`.\n- `locality(Owner)` now first calls a new `regionFromPostcode(...)` helper: if the owner's postcode falls in a known region range, that region wins. Only when the postcode is absent, non-numeric, or in no known range does it fall back to the existing `CITY_REGION` city table (`\"UNKNOWN\"` if the city isn't listed either).\n\nThis keeps the same region for known cities (their postcodes sit inside their own region's range) while disambiguating same-named cities by postcode:\n\n- `coreRegionFromPostcodeRange` \u2014 Sydney owner, postcode 2000 \u2192 `NSW` \u2713\n- `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity` \u2014 unknown city, postcode 3000 (VIC range) \u2192 `VIC` \u2713\n\nBoth tests (the full suite) pass. I left the separate `Postcodes.validate` logic untouched, since it governs write-time validation rather than read-time derivation and its behaviour is unchanged.",
