    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`, exactly as the code stands. The whole pipeline runs inside a single `transaction` governance (committed once at the end).\n\n## 0. Endpoint gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** (`owners.POST.yml` \u2192 `composition.authorize`): requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Failure \u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler.\n- **Bean-validation on the request body** (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`, runs before `BuildOwner`'s method body). Constraints from the generated DTO:\n  - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`\n  - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`\n  - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n  - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n  - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n  - `email` (optional): `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n  - `postcode` (optional): `@Pattern` `^[0-9]{4}$`\n  - Failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` handler.\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 `BuildOwner`\nSide-effects and validations, in the order they execute inside the method:\n1. **Publishes `sharesHousehold` flag** (`Out<Boolean>`) from `request.getSharesHousehold()` \u2014 separate variable, not on the entity.\n2. **Normalizes address in place**: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE` (`Addresses.normalize`).\n3. **Required-field check** (post-normalization) for `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone`; any blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**). (Runs *after* address normalization, so an address blank-once-normalized is rejected here.)\n4. **Normalizes telephone to E.164 in place** (`Telephones.toE164`): strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep `+`/country code or assume `+61` (dropping one leading `0`); must be `+` then 8\u201315 digits; `+61` must have exactly 9 national digits, `+1` exactly 10. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**).\n5. **Normalizes email in place** (optional; `OwnerEmails.normalize`): blank/null left as-is; else must match the email regex and is stored lower-cased. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (**400**).\n6. **Validates postcode** (optional; `Postcodes.validate`) against the city's region range (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any 4-digit). Out of range/non-numeric \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**).\n7. **Maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n8. **Sets `registrationDate`**: supplied value, else `LocalDate.now()`; then **rolls weekends forward** (Sat\u2192+2, Sun\u2192+1) to the next business day, stored on the entity.\n9. Publishes the built `Owner` (`Out<Owner>`).\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 `AssignHousehold`\n- Only acts if `sharesHousehold` is true; otherwise no-op.\n- Finds existing owners with the same normalized last name + normalized address.\n- **Assigns `householdId`**: reuses an existing member's id if present, else derives a deterministic `HH-` + SHA-256 prefix from last name + address.\n- **Side-effect / write**: back-fills and **saves** any matching members that lacked a `householdId`.\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 `EnsureUniqueIdentity`\n- **Duplicate check** on the whole identity key = `telephone|email|householdId` (`OwnerIdentity.key`). If any other owner has the same key \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**). (Runs after household assignment so `householdId` is part of the key.)\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode`\n- **Assigns `customerCode`** = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`: first 3 letters of city and last name upper-cased, and a per-city 4-digit sequence = (count of existing owners in that city, case-insensitive) + 1.\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 `AssignNamesakeCount`\n- **Assigns `namesakeCount`** = number of existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 `EnsureCityCapacity`\n- **Capacity check**: if the owner's city (normalized, case-insensitive) already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n## Step 7 \u2014 `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`\n- **Daily-limit check**: if \u2265 100 existing owners already share this owner's (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n\n## Step 8 \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n- **Persists** the owner (`ownerRepository.save`) \u2014 assigns the id.\n\n## Step 9 \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect**: logs an `AUDIT` line with `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and computed `membershipLevel`.\n\n## Step 10 \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- Maps to `OwnerDto` (computing derived fields: `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`) and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nNote the ordering consequence: because bean-validation and `BuildOwner`'s own required-field check run first, malformed/missing bodies are 400s before any duplicate/capacity/limit checks run; the three business-rule rejections then fire in the order duplicate (409) \u2192 city capacity (409) \u2192 daily limit (429).\n\nAny `DataIntegrityViolationException` at save, or otherwise unmatched exception, falls through to the generic `DataIntegrityViolationException` / `java.lang.Exception` handlers."
  },
